triggers:
  - id: oil-crisis
    name: Oil crises
    date: 1973-10
    row: 37
    tags: [energy, finance, society]
  - id: financial-crisis
    name: 2008 financial crisis
    date: 2008-09
    row: 137
    tags: [finance, society]
  - id: nuclear-fission
    name: Nuclear fission
    date: 1938-12
    row: 33
    tags: [energy, science]
  - id: watt-condenser
    name: Watt's separate condenser patent
    date: 1769-01
    row: 21
    tags: [energy, industry]
    description: A condenser apart from the cylinder made the steam engine efficient enough to drive factories.
  - id: wall-street-crash
    name: Wall Street Crash
    date: 1929-10
    row: 167
    tags: [finance, society]
    description: The crash that began the Great Depression, and with it the New Deal.
  - id: sputnik
    name: Sputnik 1
    date: 1957-10
    row: 63
    tags: [transport, communication]
    description: The first artificial satellite; ARPA was founded four months later.
  - id: iphone-announced
    name: iPhone announced
    date: 2007-01
    row: 79
    tags: [communication, computing]
    description: A phone that was a touch-screen computer first.
  - id: covid-pandemic
    name: COVID-19 declared a pandemic
    date: 2020-03
    row: 149
    tags: [health, society]
    description: Lockdowns sent office work home and vaccine development into months rather than years.
  - id: chatgpt-launch
    name: ChatGPT launched
    date: 2022-11
    row: 107
    tags: [computing]
    description: A chat interface to a large language model reached a hundred million users in two months.
  - id: bridgewater-canal
    name: Bridgewater Canal opens
    date: 1761-07
    row: 47
    tags: [transport, industry]
    description: A canal built to carry coal to Manchester halved its price and set off canal mania.
  - id: water-frame-patent
    name: Arkwright's water frame patent
    date: 1769-07
    row: 3
    tags: [industry]
    description: A spinning machine too large for a cottage, which put spinning into mills.
  - id: jenner-smallpox
    name: Jenner's smallpox inoculation
    date: 1796-05
    row: 149
    tags: [health, science]
    description: Edward Jenner inoculated a boy with cowpox and showed he was protected from smallpox.
  - id: voltaic-pile
    name: Volta announces the electric pile
    date: 1800-03
    row: 23
    tags: [energy, science]
    description: "The first battery: a steady electric current for anyone who stacked zinc, copper and brine."
  - id: oersted-compass
    name: Oersted's compass needle moves
    date: 1820-04
    row: 27
    tags: [science, energy]
    description: "A current deflected a compass needle: electricity and magnetism were one thing."
  - id: rainhill-trials
    name: Rainhill trials
    date: 1829-10
    row: 51
    tags: [transport]
    description: Stephenson's Rocket won the trials for the Liverpool and Manchester Railway.
  - id: faraday-induction
    name: Faraday discovers induction
    date: 1831-08
    row: 31
    tags: [science, energy]
    description: "A moving magnet made a current: the principle of the dynamo and the transformer."
  - id: daguerreotype
    name: Daguerreotype announced
    date: 1839-08
    row: 69
    tags: [communication, science]
    description: The French government bought the process and gave it to the world.
  - id: great-exhibition
    name: Great Exhibition opens
    date: 1851-05
    row: 7
    tags: [industry, society]
    description: The Crystal Palace showed interchangeable American machinery and goods on display to the public.
  - id: broad-street-pump
    name: Broad Street cholera outbreak
    date: 1854-08
    row: 153
    tags: [health, science]
    description: John Snow traced a cholera outbreak to one water pump.
  - id: drake-well
    name: Drake's oil well strikes oil
    date: 1859-08
    row: 29
    tags: [energy]
    description: The first commercial oil well, at Titusville, Pennsylvania.
  - id: telephone-patent
    name: Bell's telephone patent
    date: 1876-03
    row: 77
    tags: [communication]
    description: Patent 174,465, granted three days before the first call.
  - id: edison-lamp
    name: Edison demonstrates his lamp
    date: 1879-12
    row: 35
    tags: [energy]
    description: A carbon-filament bulb that burned for hours, shown at Menlo Park.
  - id: benz-motorwagen
    name: Benz Patent-Motorwagen patented
    date: 1886-01
    row: 59
    tags: [transport]
    description: The first car built around an internal combustion engine.
  - id: wright-flyer
    name: Wright brothers' first flight
    date: 1903-12
    row: 47
    tags: [transport]
    description: Twelve seconds of controlled, powered flight at Kitty Hawk.
  - id: model-t
    name: Ford Model T launched
    date: 1908-10
    row: 9
    tags: [industry, transport]
    description: A car for everyone, and within five years the moving assembly line that built it.
notes:
